{
  "topic": "How a rainbow forms",
  "language": "en",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "How does a rainbow form? 🌈",
  "hook": "Why does a rainbow appear, and why are its colors always in the same order?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_hook",
      "narration": "Why does a rainbow appear, and why are its colors always in the same order?",
      "on_screen_text": "How does a rainbow form?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rainbow"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_recipe",
      "narration": "You need two things to see one: the Sun behind you and raindrops in front of you.",
      "on_screen_text": "Sun behind, rain ahead",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Sun",
        "rain"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_drop",
      "narration": "Every drop works like a tiny prism: light goes in, bends, bounces off the back and comes out again.",
      "on_screen_text": "Every drop is a prism",
      "highlight_words": [
        "prism"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_split",
      "narration": "As it bends, each color comes out at a different angle: red at about forty-two degrees and violet at about forty.",
      "on_screen_text": "Red 42°, violet 40°",
      "highlight_words": [
        "42°"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_many",
      "narration": "That's why red reaches you from higher drops and violet from lower ones: red is always on top.",
      "on_screen_text": "Red is always on top",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Red"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_cone",
      "narration": "All the drops at that angle form a circle around the shadow of your head.",
      "on_screen_text": "A circle around you",
      "highlight_words": [
        "circle"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_circle",
      "narration": "From the ground the horizon cuts part of it off, but from a plane a rainbow can look like a full circle.",
      "on_screen_text": "A full circle!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "full"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_double",
      "narration": "And if light bounces twice inside the drop, a second, fainter rainbow appears with its colors reversed.",
      "on_screen_text": "The double one is reversed",
      "highlight_words": [
        "reversed"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_yours",
      "narration": "Since it all depends on where you stand, nobody sees exactly the same rainbow as you.",
      "on_screen_text": "Your rainbow is yours alone",
      "highlight_words": [
        "yours"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "arco_outro",
      "narration": "Send this to someone who always looks for rainbows.",
      "on_screen_text": "Send this to a rainbow hunter",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rainbow"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "With the Sun behind you and rain ahead, every drop acts like a prism: light enters, refracts, reflects inside and comes out split into colors, red at about 42° and violet at about 40° from the shadow of your head. From a plane it can look like a full circle, and a double rainbow has its colors reversed. Original 3D animation; angles exaggerated for clarity.",
